when onEntryChange fires, that the Stack options include a live_preview block with enable=true, and that the content state merges incoming preview data correctly.","suggestedFix":"Create test/unit/context/contentstackContext.test.tsx with vitest tests verifying: (1) ContentstackProvider initializes content from defaultContent, (2) onEntryChange callback merges updated entries into content state, (3) useContent returns updated content after onEntryChange fires."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/hooks/useContent.ts","line":5,"description":"useContent calls useContext(ContentstackContext) but there is no reactive Provider component supplying a changing value. The hook will always return a static value and cannot propagate live preview updates to the 236+ consumers. Even if Contentstack live preview events fired, there is no state setter to trigger re-renders.","suggestedFix":"Once the ContentstackProvider with reactive useState is implemented in contentstackContext.tsx, useContent will automatically benefit from the reactive context value. No change needed in useContent itself — the fix is in the Provider."},{"severity":"major","file":"pages/api/preview.ts","line":1,"description":"No pages/api/preview.ts route exists to enable Next.js draft mode. Without this, getStaticProps will not re-run on CMS edits and the live preview session cannot be established server-side. No context.preview or context.previewData is forwarded to Contentstack service calls in any page component.","suggestedFix":"Create pages/api/preview.ts that calls res.setPreviewData({}) to enable Next.js draft mode, and update getStaticProps in page components to forward context.preview and live_preview URL params to getSingleEntry/getEntry/findSingletonEntry service calls."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":95,"description":"The Stack options do include a live_preview config block (host, management_token, enable: true) which is correct. However, createContentTypeQuery and createContentTypeEntryQuery do not pass live_preview hash data from URL params to the Contentstack query chain. Even if the Stack is configured for live preview, queries will always return published content because the live_preview hash from the URL is never forwarded to the query.","suggestedFix":"Add an optional live_preview field to ICreateQueryConfig and ICreateEntryConfig interfaces, and pass it through to the Contentstack query chain in createContentTypeQuery and createContentTypeEntryQuery so that draft content is fetched when a live_preview hash is present."}],"summary":"The prescribed minimal fix for Live Preview of Content in CMS was NOT implemented. The critical chokepoint — src/context/contentstackContext.tsx — still exports a bare createContext with no reactive Provider component, no useState, no useEffect, and no onEntryChange subscription. The useContent hook consumed by 236+ components will always return static SSR content. The @contentstack/live-preview-utils SDK is not installed. No vitest tests exist. No pages/api/preview.ts route exists for Next.js draft mode. While the Stack options do correctly include a live_preview config block (enable: true, host, management_token), this alone is insufficient — without a reactive Provider subscribing to SDK events, no live preview updates can ever reach any consumer. The implementation must be rejected and the prescribed minimal fix applied."}
